      "text": "Correction: Around 0:40 you say that part of Kiribati is Micronesia while the rest is \"geographically and culturally\" Polynesia. I'm pretty sure that is not accurate. You should check me on this, but my understanding is that the eastern two thirds are Kiribati are well within the Polynesian Triangle geographically, but they were uninhabited until the European era and they brought people from the Micronesian Gilbert Islands of Kiribati to live there. So that eastern part of Kiribati is still culturally Micronesian, even if geographically Polynesian. Feel free to doublecheck me and let me know if I'm wrong. Congrats on getting the pronunciation right though!",
